# AddressSanitizer suppressions for running the GUI under ASan.
#
# NOT for the test suite, which needs none of this - desktop_tests is clean.
# This exists because the application links the XCB platform plugin, and
# libxcb-cursor allocates a 21-byte buffer and then strchr()s past the end of
# it while loading the window's cursor. The whole allocation and the whole read
# are inside that library; our only frame in the report is w.show().
#
# Suppressed rather than investigated again: it is reached from
# QWindowPrivate::applyCursor() on every show(), so without this every ASan run
# of the application aborts before the window appears, and the one class of bug
# ASan is here to find - ours - never gets a chance to show up.
#
# Usage:
#   ASAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tools/asan.supp:detect_leaks=0 ./romanian_whist_desktop
#
# NOTE WHAT detect_leaks=0 DOES THERE: it turns off leak detection ENTIRELY,
# ours included - it is not narrowing anything to the bug this file suppresses,
# which is what suppressions= is for. It is in the usual command because Qt and
# XCB leak on exit by design and the report buries everything else. Drop it when
# you are actually hunting a leak:
#
#   ASAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tools/asan.supp ./romanian_whist_desktop
#
# See docs/LOCAL_VERIFICATION.md, "Running the APPLICATION under ASan".
interceptor_via_lib:libxcb-cursor
